{
  "info": {
    "name": "Market Propiedades - API",
    "description": "Colección para probar el backend local. El login guarda el token automáticamente en la variable {{accessToken}}, así las requests siguientes lo usan solas.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3002" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "marco.silvaponce10@gmail.com" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "cambia-esta-contrasena-min-8-chars" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (correcto)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Si las credenciales son correctas, devuelve { accessToken }. El script de Tests (pestaña abajo en Postman) guarda ese token en la variable de colección para las demás requests."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve accessToken', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "",
                  "if (body.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "  console.log('Token guardado en {{accessToken}}');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (password incorrecta)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"password-que-no-es\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Mismo endpoint, contraseña mala a propósito. Tiene que devolver 401 con el mismo mensaje genérico que si el email tampoco existiera."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (con token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }]
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
            "description": "Usa el token guardado por 'Login (correcto)'. Corré esa primero. Devuelve el usuario que JwtStrategy encontró en la base a partir del `sub` del token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve el email correcto', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('adminEmail'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (sin token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
            "description": "A propósito sin Authorization header. Tiene que devolver 401 — JwtAuthGuard corta antes de llegar al controller."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 401 sin token', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
